comments.body:
**Claim to prove.** The result holds in all degenerate configurations; each must be explicitly dispatched (faithfulness to 'for every two-state ensemble on an arbitrary finite-dimensional Hilbert space'):
- $p_1=0$ or $p_2=0$ ($I_{\mathrm{acc}}=0$, trivially projective);
- $\rho_1=\rho_2$ ($I_{\mathrm{acc}}=0$);
- $\rho_1,\rho_2$ commuting (classical: common eigenbasis is projective-optimal);
- supports of $\rho_1,\rho_2$ not spanning $\mathcal H$ (restrict, then complete the projective measurement on the complement);
- $d=1$.

**Why needed.** These cases are easy but mandatory; omitting them leaves the universal quantifier unproven.
